# Staged counterfactual arm directories (launch_arm.sh) and counterfactual builds
code/arm1/
code/arm2/
code/arm3/
code/cf/
code/data/
code/trans_bench_to_tf/
code/trans_*/
code/tr/
# build output directories: three binaries, a generated source copy and the
# compiler's .err files, all reproduced by build_transition.sh in 90 seconds.
# tr75/ holds the windowed build used to validate the T=75 memory fix.
code/tr75/
code/tr[0-9]*/
# Transition RUN directories. stage_transition.sh copies both steady states in,
# so one is 4.4 GB of .dat before the run writes a line. code/trans_*/ already
# covers the ones named trans_*; a run named for its horizon and arm is not.
code/t[0-9]*_*/
# The benchmark's own run directory and build output, on the same rule as the
# arm directories above. bm/ holds the cold-start benchmark solve: its binary,
# its handover (the seed for it is committed at code/seeds/) and the ~2.2 GB of
# *baseline_benchmark.* files the arm and the transition read. bmbuild/ is the
# three benchmark binaries and the compiler's .err files, reproduced in 100
# seconds. Neither can go in git and the largest single file is 295 MB against
# GitHub's 100 MB limit.
code/bm/
code/bmbuild/

# GENERATED TRANSITION AND BENCHMARK BUILD DIRECTORIES. build_transition_gf.sh,
# build_cf.sh and the hand-staged benchmark build each write a generated .f90
# plus three binaries into their own directory, so that a run cannot tread on
# another's .dat files. The generator plus the master source reproduces every one
# of them exactly, and a committed copy would go stale against the master
# silently -- which is the same reasoning the variant_*.f90 rule above gives.
code/bm_build/
code/tr_gf/
code/tr_gf5/
code/tr_gf*/
code/tr_nogf*/
code/cf/
code/bench/
