# The scan seed is COMMITTED on purpose: it is the converged benchmark,
# compressed, so a session of its own can run a scan point. Added with -f.
!code/scan_seed/

# Scan POINT directories: a 253 MB distribution and a binary each, like every
# other run directory. code/scan_seed/ is the exception -- it is the committed
# 14 MB compressed benchmark the points warm start from, and the negation below
# must stay AFTER this pattern to survive it.
code/scan_*/
!code/scan_seed/
!code/scan_seed/**
# the one-class seed for the omega_c = 0.7 sensitivity (9 October), committed on the same rule
!code/scan_seed_1c/
!code/scan_seed_1c/**

# Welfare-pass run directories, on the same rule as the scan points: each holds
# a raw 265 MB calibration_distribution1.dat and a binary. A raw distribution
# must never reach the branch -- GitHub rejects any blob over 100 MB, so one
# stray `git add -A` here would wedge the push for everyone. The gzipped
# artefacts belong under results/, as code/scan_seed/ does.
code/welfare_*/

# The full-homelessness-internalisation run directory, on the same rule as every
# other run directory above: a 265 MB distribution, a 24 MB second distribution
# and a 3 MB binary, all reproduced by remote_internalise_point.sh stage from the
# committed scan_seed/. The record of the run is its log and its handover vector,
# not the grids it leaves behind.
code/internalise_h_oc006/

# The 12-block companion of the run directory above, launched fresh from the
# seed with frozen_stop_after_blocks 12 so the run leaves the calibration loop
# and reaches save_welfare_curve. Same rule and same reason: the distributions
# and the binary are reproduced by remote_internalise_point12.sh from the
# committed scan_seed/, and the record of the run is its log and its handover.
code/internalise_h_oc006_b12/
